@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Image lineage — parent tags, ensure.sh modes, and the publish contract

node "defs/ build scripts" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "proveo_image_ref\n<env-var> <repo> <tag>" as REF <<app>>
  component "proveo_ref_tag\n<ref> → tag (default latest)" as RTAG <<app>>
  component "<parent>/ensure.sh\n--tag <t> [--push]" as ENSURE <<app>>
  component "proveo_require_published\nregistry probe + advisory" as REQ <<app>>
}

folder "Lineage" as CHAIN <<host>> {
  component "proveo/base" as B <<app>>
  component "proveo/base-node" as BN <<app>>
  component "proveo/base-node-lsp" as BNL <<app>>
  component "proveo/base-node-browser" as BNB <<app>>
  component "cecli · cursor" as H1 <<app>>
  component "opencode · claudecode" as H2 <<app>>
  component "claudecode-solidity" as H3 <<app>>
}

node "Tag policy" as TAGS <<host>> {
  component "proveo build\n--load → :local (never :latest)" as BUILD <<app>>
  component "proveo deploy\nrequire :local → retag → --push" as DEPLOY <<app>>
  component "maintain.ResolveImage\nnewer of :local / :latest" as RESOLVE <<app>>
  component "proveo_resolve_image\nthe same rule, in shell" as SHRESOLVE <<app>>
}

node "defs/**/test.sh · tests/helpers.sh" as DEFTESTS <<host>>

cloud "Registry" as REG <<cloud>>
component "A published image shadowing\nthe build under test" as SHADOW <<error>>
component "Unpublished parent\non a --push build" as FAIL <<error>>

B ARROW_MAIN BN
BN ARROW_MAIN BNL
BNL ARROW_MAIN BNB
B ARROW_MAIN H1
BNL ARROW_MAIN H2
H2 ARROW_MAIN H3

REF ARROW_MAIN CHAIN : every ""BASE_IMAGE"" at the CHILD'S tag
RTAG ARROW_MAIN REF : derive the tag from the image being built
ENSURE ARROW_MAIN CHAIN : local — present · floor · pull · build
ENSURE ARROW_CLOUD REQ : ""--push"" — publication is all that matters
REQ ARROW_CLOUD REG : ""buildx imagetools inspect""
REQ ARROW_ERROR FAIL : fail early, at the declaration site
BUILD ARROW_MAIN RESOLVE : ""<image>:local""
BUILD ARROW_MAIN DEPLOY : the tested image
DEPLOY ARROW_CLOUD REG : promoted, multi-arch
RESOLVE ARROW_ERROR SHADOW : prevented by tag, not by luck
REG ARROW_ERROR SHADOW : sbx re-pulls at sandbox creation
DEFTESTS ARROW_MAIN SHRESOLVE : resolve before the first ""docker run""
SHRESOLVE ARROW_MAIN RESOLVE : one rule, pinned by\n""TestShellImageResolverMatchesResolveImage""

note right of REF
  **A child never hardcodes ""latest"".** Every parent reference is
  resolved through one helper, so ""proveo deploy all --tag v2""
  publishes ""proveo/<harness>:v2"" built ""FROM proveo/base:v2"". Left
  hardcoded, the published lineage silently mixes two releases and
  nothing in the image records it.

  A ""PROVEO_*_IMAGE"" override wins outright — it is a complete ref
  chosen by the caller, so the tag is not reapplied to it.
end note

note bottom of ENSURE
  **The two modes answer different questions.**

  ""--tag"" (local ""--load""): is the parent present at this tag with a
  usable floor? Present + floor → done; else pull; else build from
  source. A tag alone is not enough — a stale image from a different
  lineage looks present but has the wrong contents, so each ensure.sh
  runs a floor probe (the tools that layer must provide).

  ""--push"": the child resolves the parent from the REGISTRY, so the
  local pull/floor dance answers the wrong question entirely and is
  skipped. Only publication matters.
end note

note bottom of REQ
  **Deploying one target whose parents are unpublished is not
  supported.** The scripts refuse to publish a parent as a side effect
  of a child's deploy — that would push an image the caller never
  asked for, and (for claudecode-solidity) a local ""docker image
  inspect"" would be interrogating the wrong store while the build
  resolves from the registry.

  Failing at the declaration site turns a bare 'failed to resolve
  source metadata … not found' 30 seconds into the build into an
  actionable message naming ""proveo deploy all"" and the parent target.
end note

note right of CHAIN
  **Each layer exists where it does so its consumers can decline it.**

  | layer | holds | why not lower |
  | ""proveo/base"" | git · gh · ca-certs · curl · jq · dumb-init · bash · tmux · ""proveo-entrypoint"" · the harden pass | the universally-shared floor, and **no language runtime** |
  | ""proveo/base-node"" | Node + pnpm + Bun | cursor and cecli would otherwise carry a Node runtime they never call |
  | ""proveo/base-node-lsp"" | the language servers ""_lsp_server()"" can run | a non-LSP Node consumer should not pay for them |
  | ""proveo/base-node-browser"" | Playwright + Chromium + agent-browser + ~150 apt libs | only browser-capable harnesses need it |
  | ""claudecode-solidity"" | Foundry · solc-select · solhint · semgrep | ~1.5 GB of toolchain, on the one harness that audits contracts |

  **Two size lessons are baked into the shape.** The Solidity toolchain was
  split out because it alone doubled the harness image; and its per-user
  toolchains are installed **once, as the runtime user** — the earlier
  root-install-then-copy-to-home pattern shipped the 400 MB toolkit twice
  in one image.

  **The browser layer pins Playwright deliberately.** CLI, driver and the
  installed browser must move together — a mismatch surfaces as "can't
  locate browser executables" rather than as a version error. The browser
  store is shared and world-readable because the harness never runs as
  root: an arbitrary run-as uid has to be able to launch Chromium, and a
  repo-local Playwright honours the same variable, so a project's own
  ""npx playwright install"" lands in the same place. agent-browser is
  pinned the same way (version + tarball digest) and pointed at that
  store through a revision-stable symlink, so the layer holds ONE
  Chromium for two clients (_spec/defs/browser-layer.puml).

  Every layer that runs apt or npm re-runs the harden pass over the
  prefixes it touched, because a new package can reintroduce a setuid
  binary.
end note


note bottom of CHAIN
  **""proveo deploy all"" is the coherent publish path.** The maintainer
  registry is hand-ordered bases-first, then harnesses alphabetically,
  so every parent is published before its children — including
  claudecode before claudecode-solidity. Alphabetical order satisfying
  that last pair is a coincidence, not a declared edge.

  ""runPlan"" stops at the first failure, so a mid-fleet failure leaves a
  partially published set.
end note
note bottom of ENSURE
  **Every def carries the same two-script pair, and the chain is what makes
  a single build work from cold.** A ""build\.sh"" builds exactly its own
  image and calls its parent's ""ensure\.sh"" first; that parent's build in
  turn chains its own parent's. So building any harness from a clean machine
  walks the lineage upward once, and no script needs to know the whole
  chain — only its immediate parent.

  Build context is the repo root for every def, because variant Dockerfiles
  resolve ""COPY"" paths from there; a def-local context would break the
  shared ""packages/lib"" copies.
end note


note top of BUILD
  **A local build never writes ""latest"".** That
  tag means published, and while one name covered
  both, anything re-resolving the reference could
  serve the registry artifact over the build under
  test, with nothing recording which one ran.
end note

note bottom of DEPLOY
  **Deploy promotes; it never builds blind.** It
  requires ""<image>:local"" and retags that image
  before pushing, so publishing without a local
  build refuses rather than shipping something
  nothing was ever run against.
end note

note top of RESOLVE
  **Recency decides, not existence.** A stale
  local image must not shadow one just pulled, and
  a build from a minute ago must not lose to the
  registry, so the runtime compares build times
  and names which image actually won.
end note

note bottom of SHADOW
  **The sandbox backend re-pulls by reference.**
  sbx resolves the image at creation and takes it
  from the registry, so a week-old published tag
  reached the container while every local rebuild
  appeared to succeed and changed nothing.
end note

note bottom of SHRESOLVE
  **The def suites had the shadow the runtime was spared.** Every
  ""test\.sh"" and ""tests/helpers\.sh"" defaulted to ""<image>:latest"" —
  a tag ""proveo_docker_build"" REFUSES to write locally — so the only
  image they could ever reach was whatever the registry last
  published. ""mise run test-images"" read as a verdict on the working
  tree and was a verdict on the last deploy.

  Measured: ""defs/cecli/test\.sh"" failed
  ""proveo\.agent\.version label missing"" against a ""proveo/cecli:latest""
  pulled from the registry, built 2026-08-31 — three days before the
  label was added to the Dockerfile. The suite was right, the image
  was old, and nothing on the path could have produced a newer one.

  Ten sites carried it (four harnesses, their browser and solidity
  variants, the mitmproxy sidecar). They now share
  ""proveo_resolve_image"", and ""proveo_test_image"" NAMES the winner the
  way the runner does — because an image silently resolving to a
  published artifact is invisible until something behaves like code
  nobody wrote. ""build\.sh"" keeps its ""latest"" default: publishing is
  what that tag is for.
end note

@enduml
